{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/793118-a-couple-of-questions-about-the-new-investigation-system","id":793118,"title":"A couple of questions about the new investigation system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-26T08:53:01-08:00","id":793118,"title":"A couple of questions about the new investigation system","content":"The investigation rules are a fantastic way to avoid two typical pitfalls Storytellers may be challenged with when telling an investigation story: a story too linear when the players are lead from scene 1, 2, 3 etc in order to pile up information about the case ; and the risk that the players can't add the dots as efficiently as the storyteller predicted. Needless to say, I love them and I will use them in my next game session (oops, Chapter ^^). <br /> This being said, I'm facing two problems with the rules as written and I'd love your input (experience maybe) on the matter.<br /> <br /> First off intervals. Setting them is a combination of what the players are actually trying to do and the needs of the story. Let's say, the Characters have to uncover the nest of diabolists rampaging the city. They are fast and furious, always on the move, quite hard to catch and thus I set the number of Clues at 3 and, for the sake of the story (because time is of the essence in order to avoid more casualties) I fix the interval at one night. What if the players decide to go faster, by splitting up for instance ?<br /> <br /> Last but not least I have a problem with the final step. Suppose the characters manage to uncover 3 clues, one of which is incomplete. If they uncover the truth now, they will fall short as they will have 2 Elements to solve the case instead of three and I will add one complication (the Diabolists are waiting for them for instance). But do they have the choice to continue the investigation in order to pile up three complete Elements and to solve the case without any complication ? or is it that, once they accumulate the required number of Clues, they have to uncover the truth, regardless of any Element that might be tainted or incomplete ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:06:50-08:00","id":793123,"title":"","content":"Whenever the players try to upset the story phasing, add complications to their methods. Don't be afraid to take a break to come up with said complications, saying that you need to come up with something.<br /> <br /> The inverse is also true: If you need to move on with the story, wave some rolls, or don't apply as many penalties as usual.<br /> <br /> I usually consider having more clues around than the expressly necessary to uncover the truth. If they squander them too, that's on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:20:09-08:00","id":793135,"title":"","content":"Thanks, it helps a lot and adding more Clues than strictly necessary is a nice way to simulate how hard the investigation actually is. And do you tell your players? Do you say &quot;there are four Clues to uncover but only three are mandatory to solve the case without any complication ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:33:36-08:00","id":793143,"title":"","content":"No, only when they've actually exhausted all their efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:50:40-08:00","id":793157,"title":"","content":"Assume that competent playergroup will succeed on discovering around 75% of clues, so it's nice to have extra 25% of the target number as safety buffer. 10 clues required to solve the mystery? Plan for 13 being around; this way they can fuck up 3 of them, and if they don't, then they can spend them safely, <br /> And if they have proper setup for extra elements (like skills at 4, Investigative Prodigy, Invst Aide), they can actually get more. Don't sweat that, because they will probably use them to get + on their rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:55:32-08:00","id":793161,"title":"","content":"I haven't used the system yet, but I think for me it would depend on the nature and stakes of the investigation. Like, if you're researching a ritual to summon a powerful infernal entity or something, sure, gather as many clues as you want until you feel confident you have enough information to perform the ritual safely. But if you're trying to find the identity of a serial killer before they get to their next victim, you don't have time to keep looking for more clues once you've got enough to catch the killer. People's lives are at stake, you can look for more clues <i>after</i> you've got this bastard in custody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:26:25-08:00","id":793178,"title":"","content":"That's the investigation we're having now: they have to locate two Belial's Brood Forsworns before they kill more vampires in Aurora, Illinois. So, in this instance I'm not very preoccupied: if they take their sweet time, more kindred will turn up dead and, eventually, the Brood will live town and they'll miss them.<br /> <br /> Now, reading about your answers, it seems:<br /> <br /> 1) when you uncover all Clues you will have to uncover the truth but you can lay out there more.Clues than strictly necessary (saying that a competent troupe will succeed at 75% and thus add 25% extra Clues if you want this to run smoothly and less if you want it to be challenging, sounds great)<br /> 2) You can fine tune the difficulty by putting more or less Clues than necessary. If you need 3 Clues, putting 4 would be easy and 5 piece of cake, if you put three it might be challenging, if you put only two it will be darn hard as you will have at least one complication (unless you have a specialist involved).<br /> 3) Playing on intervals is also a good way to adjust the difficulty, especially when there is a timer: the serial killer is after your wife now and he's killing every Saturday and we are Thursday, you'd better hurry up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T12:01:00-08:00","id":793219,"title":"","content":"If you handled out too many clues, you may consider seducing your players into burning them for some cool perks; instead of standard &quot;burn this for +2 to a roll&quot;, offer them something more unique. This way you can make your players slow down their investigation on their own, without you having to &quot;cheat&quot; and add higher Clues requirement for solving the mystery.By unique perks I mean &quot;effects that are not represented by a bonus to dice roll, and if they were represented in mechanics, they would be represented by one-shot application of a merit&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T13:34:31-08:00","id":793250,"title":"","content":"I love this idea, so let's say I might &quot;lure&quot; my players into using an Element in an attempt to find the Diabolists' lair instead of their hunting ground. That would take one more night, make more casualties, but it will be safer for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}